# Delete the branch after the PR

When a pull request into `develop` or `main` is merged, delete its head branch. GitHub deletes the remote branch on merge.

After the merge, update the base and delete the local branch:

```bash
git switch develop
git pull --ff-only
git branch -d feature/the-branch
```

Do not delete `main` or `develop`. Do not delete `release/*` while that release is still open. Do not delete a branch that still has commits absent from its base.
